@startuml mo_bill_flow
title Missouri General Assembly: how a bill becomes law

|Originating chamber|
start
note right
  Either chamber can originate a bill
  (HB / SB). Budget bills (HB 1-13+)
  start in the House by custom.
  House: 163 members, majority 82, 2/3 = 109
  Senate: 34 members, majority 18, 2/3 = 23
end note
:Introduced, 1st reading;
:2nd reading, referred to committee;
if (Committee reports "do pass"?) then (yes)
  :Often as a substitute (HCS / SCS);
else (no)
  :Bill dies in committee;
  stop
endif
if (House?) then (yes)
  :Perfection: floor amendments,
  voice vote to perfect;
else (Senate)
  :Floor debate and amendments
  (unlimited debate: filibusters
  can stall or kill the bill);
endif
:3rd reading and final passage
(recorded roll call, constitutional majority);

|Other chamber|
:1st reading, 2nd reading, committee;
:3rd reading and final passage
(recorded roll call);
if (Passed unchanged?) then (yes)
else (amended / substitute,\ne.g. SS for HB)
  |Originating chamber|
  if (Concur in the changes?) then (yes)
    :Adopt the other chamber's version
    (roll call);
  else (no)
    :Refuse to concur,
    request conference;
    |Conference committee|
    :Conferees from each chamber
    negotiate one text (CCS);
    :Conference report (CCR);
    |Originating chamber|
    :Adopt CCR, 3rd reading
    and final passage;
    |Other chamber|
    :Adopt CCR, 3rd reading
    and final passage;
  endif
endif

|Originating chamber|
:"Truly Agreed To and Finally Passed" (TAFP);
:Signed by the Speaker and the
President Pro Tem in open session;
note right
  Deadline for passage: 6 p.m. on the Friday
  after the second Monday in May.
  Joint resolutions (HJR / SJR) skip the
  governor and go to the ballot.
end note

|Governor|
if (Governor acts?) then (sign)
  :Signed into law;
elseif () then (no action in time)
  :Becomes law without signature;
else (veto / line-item veto\non appropriations)
  :Returned with objections;
  |Originating chamber|
  :Veto session (September):
  vote to override (2/3);
  |Other chamber|
  if (2/3 in both chambers?) then (yes)
    :Veto overridden;
  else (no)
    :Veto stands;
    stop
  endif
endif

|Governor|
:Takes effect August 28,
or immediately with an emergency
clause (2/3 in each chamber);
stop
@enduml
